What CC BY 4.0 covers
---------------------

- The generated data: the published runs in data/ (the day zips and data/runs/manifest.json)
  and the tables in data/halvern/, and the month released as medianville_2027-03_month.zip.
- systems-lens/blocks.json: the mapped blocks, their circumstances, patterns and loops.
- The hand-written records: sim/detailed_overrides.csv, sim/detailed_sample.csv and
  sim/detail_parts/, data/halvern/detailed_overrides.csv, data/halvern/detailed_sample_500.csv
  and data/halvern/detail_parts/, and the copies inside the zips.
- The pages for agents: llms.txt, llms-full.txt and agents/.
- The documents: the READMEs, story/ (the decision log, the run records and the other
  documents), and the evidence results in sim/evidence/results/.
- The images and video in this folder: the screenshots in story/ and archive/,
  thumbnail.webp and preview.mp4.


What it does not cover
----------------------

- evidence/ is under neither license. It holds third-party material: quotes, sources,
  findings drawn from them and citations. Each quote and source belongs to its author or
  publisher.
- The code is under the Mozilla Public License 2.0, the repository's license (see LICENSE at
  the repository root): sim/ (the simulator and its tests, except the hand-written records
  above), tools/, sources/tools/, the copies of the simulator inside the zips and in
  data/halvern/, and the pages' HTML, JavaScript and CSS (index.html, about/, explorer/,
  systems-lens/, archive/, real-day.js, runs.js and sound.js).
- fflate.js is fflate by Arjun Barrett and contributors, under the MIT License
  (https://github.com/101arrowz/fflate).
- The public datasets that sources/ lists and derives tables from keep their publishers'
  terms, recorded in the license_or_terms column of sources/manifest.csv.


How to attribute
----------------

Cite as: James, J. (2026). Medianville: a simulated American city's transactions
[synthetic dataset]. https://medianville.netlify.app/ Data under CC BY 4.0.

Please also say that the data is synthetic: every person, household, business and street is
invented, and no record describes a real person or place. The license cannot require that;
the project asks it (https://medianville.netlify.app/llms.txt).
